  "explanation": "H is defined as `(H\u2086.restrictScalars (ZMod 2)).map l`. `Submodule.mem_map` states `x \u2208 map f p \u2194 \u2203 y, y \u2208 p \u2227 f y = x`. Take f = l and p = H\u2086.restrictScalars (ZMod 2). Membership in `restrictScalars` is definitionally membership in H\u2086, and `\u2203 y \u2208 H\u2086, l y = x` unfolds to `\u2203 y, y \u2208 H\u2086 \u2227 l y = x`. So `Submodule.mem_map` closes the goal up to unfolding H and restrictScalars. If `exact` doesn't see through the definitions, `by simp [H, Submodule.mem_map]` should work. The library's own proof is `Iff.rfl`, which doesn't name the lemma.",
